Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: use noncoherent SROOT DMA on the audited P16 BIOS

ASUS ProArt P16 H7607BA BIOS .300 omits ROT0._CCA. Its live IORT
nevertheless routes the NVDA8600 revision-1 device through SMMUv3
0x14900000, Stream ID 1, with noncoherent memory properties. The
Windows nvsrootmbx provider explicitly requests MmNonCached memory
for its bounded DMA common buffer.

Treat only this missing-attribute case as noncoherent before normal
platform DMA configuration. Preserve explicit/inherited attributes,
other revisions and other machines. Do not borrow DLA0's coherent
DMA device or bypass the firmware-declared IOMMU route.

Experimental: patch application, policy cases and compilation have
been checked. Physical DMA and boot verification remain pending.
This patch is not installed in the running kernel.

---
diff --git a/drivers/acpi/scan.c b/drivers/acpi/scan.c
--- a/drivers/acpi/scan.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/scan.c
@@ -1707,7 +1707,29 @@
 					       NULL, &cca);
 		if (ACPI_SUCCESS(status))
 			adev->flags.cca_seen = 1;
-		else if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED))
+		else if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED) &&
+			 status == AE_NOT_FOUND &&
+			 dmi_match(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "ASUS") &&
+			 dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "ProArt P16 H7607BA") &&
+			 dmi_match(DMI_BIOS_VERSION, "H7607BA.300") &&
+			 !strcmp(acpi_device_hid(adev), "NVDA8600")) {
+			unsigned long long revision;
+
+			/* This BIOS omits ROT0._CCA despite its IORT DMA mapping.
+			 * IORT declares noncoherent memory, Stream ID 1 through
+			 * SMMUv3 0x14900000. The Windows SROOT provider requests
+			 * an explicitly noncached common buffer. Keep the normal
+			 * ACPI/IORT DMA path and architecture cache maintenance;
+			 * do not borrow DLA0's coherent DMA device/domain.
+			 */
+			if (ACPI_SUCCESS(acpi_evaluate_integer(adev->handle,
+						 "_HRV", NULL, &revision)) &&
+			    revision == 1) {
+				adev->flags.cca_seen = 1;
+				acpi_handle_info(adev->handle,
+					"P16 BIOS .300 SROOT: using noncoherent DMA\n");
+			}
+		} else if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ACPI_CCA_REQUIRED))
 			/*
 			 * If architecture does not specify that _CCA is
 			 * required for DMA-able devices (e.g. x86),
